        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.sandevistan.title", "Sandevistan Acceleration");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.sandevistan.badge", "NEURAL ACCELERATION");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.sandevistan.subtitle", "Act between your enemies' reactions. Speed, perception and neurological consequences.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.sandevistan.controls", "Install a functional Sandevistan in your operating-system slot at a Ripper Station. Press the operating-system ability key (V by default) to engage or disengage. Manual cancellation keeps the activation cost and recovery period.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.sandevistan.dilation", "Nearby hostile mobs move, think, attack and wind up more slowly. Fully recovered melee strikes can connect at your accelerated attack rate against affected mobs. Incoming arrows, tridents and supported thrown projectiles advance physically in smaller steps and still collide and inflict damage. Your own and other accelerated users' shots retain their speed.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.sandevistan.multiplayer", "Time dilation is local. Other players keep normal controls; accelerated users cannot freeze one another. Overlapping fields use the strongest effect. World time, redstone and distant encounters continue normally. Bosses and encounter-specific projectiles are exempt.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.sandevistan.maintenance", "Condition reduces efficiency and active duration. Every engagement causes wear and adds existing neurological instability. Repeated activations within the recovery window add further strain. Repair the implant at a Repair Station; a broken device cannot activate.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.sandevistan.recovery", "Cooldown reductions help set the recovery period when you engage, but subsequent refunds cannot erase the hardware recovery floor. Cancelling, changing dimensions, dying or reconnecting does not reset that recovery. Consecutive-use pressure gradually decays while you rest.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.sandevistan.overload", "Overload is a predictable danger of repeated unsafe use or severe damage, not a random first-use failure. It ends acceleration, damages the implant, inflicts a short physical aftershock and doubles recovery. Medical suppression does not erase usage history.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.sandevistan.models", "Dynalar is forgiving; Zetatech rewards airborne movement; Falcon sustains aggressive combat; Warp Dancer favors precision; Apogee combines strong acceleration with bounded kill rewards. At most six distinct hostile takedowns reward Falcon or Apogee, and active time cannot exceed 150% of its initial duration.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.sandevistan.experimental", "Militech Experimental Sandevistan is a legendary-cache prototype inspired by David Martinez. It can also be fabricated after learning its design and obtaining the restricted parts. It offers intense acceleration with high strain and wear; no flight, teleportation, automatic critical hits or damage immunity.");
        add("wiki.cyberneticenhancements.sandevistan.options", "Afterimages, edge pulses, FOV and sound volume have separate client presentation settings. Disabling them does not weaken the ability. Server balance and upgrade datapacks control gameplay.");
        add("tooltip.cyberneticenhancements.special.chrome_compressor", "Pure utility operating system. No active ability; it exists to maximize chrome headroom.");
